From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:34:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ntfs: a short write does not leave the file longer than what
 was written

ntfs_file_write_iter() extends the data size and the initialized size to
pos + count before it copies the data, and takes them back only when the
write fails with nothing written. When the copy stops early and the
write returns fewer bytes than asked for, as a buffered write does when
the volume fills up in the middle of it, both sizes stay at pos + count:
the file is longer than what was written, by a tail of zeros that no
write put there, and nothing reports it. The writer is told that only
part was written, and its next write fails with ENOSPC, but the size on
the disk says otherwise. On a 64 MiB volume filled by 1 MiB writes, the
last write wrote 565248 of 1048576 bytes and the file was left 483328
bytes longer than that, all zeros (the disk was filled with 0xa5 before
mkntfs, so it is not old data), before and after a remount; ntfsck found
nothing wrong, since the sizes agree with each other. With this change
the file ends at the last byte written and reads back as written.

On a short write, take the initialized size and then the data size back
to iocb->ki_pos (or to what they were, if that is more), the way the
error path takes them back to where they were. The same order and
locks: the shrink clamps the initialized size to the data size, so it
runs only once the initialized size is right, and a failure marks the
volume as having errors.

Mainline has the same code (v7.4-rc2 and master of 2026-11-11); not
sent upstream yet.
---
 fs/ntfs/file.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/ntfs/file.c b/fs/ntfs/file.c
index 16ed53c28a1f..8ab48efa85a8 100644
--- a/fs/ntfs/file.c
+++ b/fs/ntfs/file.c
@@ -737,6 +737,40 @@ out:
 				   init_err ?: data_err);
 		}
 
+		filemap_invalidate_unlock(vi->i_mapping);
+	} else if (ret > 0 && ret < count) {
+		/*
+		 * A short write: the sizes were extended to pos + count
+		 * above, but only the bytes up to iocb->ki_pos were
+		 * written. Take the sizes back to that point, as the error
+		 * path above takes them back to where they were; otherwise
+		 * the file keeps a tail that no write put there.
+		 */
+		loff_t init_to = max(old_init_size, iocb->ki_pos);
+		loff_t data_to = max(old_data_size, iocb->ki_pos);
+		int init_err = 0;
+		int data_err = 0;
+
+		filemap_invalidate_lock(vi->i_mapping);
+		if (NInoNonResident(ni) && ni->initialized_size > init_to) {
+			mutex_lock(&ni->mrec_lock);
+			init_err = ntfs_attr_set_initialized_size(ni, init_to);
+			mutex_unlock(&ni->mrec_lock);
+		}
+		if (ni->data_size > data_to && !init_err) {
+			truncate_setsize(vi, data_to);
+			mutex_lock(&ni->mrec_lock);
+			data_err = __ntfs_attr_truncate_vfs(ni, data_to, data_to);
+			mutex_unlock(&ni->mrec_lock);
+			if (data_err)
+				i_size_write(vi, ni->data_size);
+		}
+		if (init_err || data_err) {
+			NVolSetErrors(vol);
+			ntfs_error(vi->i_sb,
+				   "Failed to trim the size after a short write: %d",
+				   init_err ?: data_err);
+		}
 		filemap_invalidate_unlock(vi->i_mapping);
 	}
 out_lock:
